  "id": "DrugBank_DB00716 - MONDO_4784",
  "verbalization": "Nedocromil is associated with Allergic Asthma through a chain of indications that link it to Asthma, which in turn is linked to Ibudilast and then to Allergic Asthma. This suggests a potential pathway where Nedocromil may influence the expression or management of Asthma, potentially through interactions with Ibudilast. The evidence from the three paths indicates that Nedocromil is involved in the pathophysiology of Allergic Asthma, possibly by modulating pathways that are also targeted by Ibudilast. The shared indication of Asthma in all three paths highlights a possible overlap in the mechanisms or clinical applications of Nedocromil and Ibudilast. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Nedocromil may contribute to the development or treatment of Allergic Asthma, though further research is needed to clarify the exact mechanism of action.",
